1917: The Text-Based Adventure Game
By: John Cherny
Lastest Update: 11/16/2026
Version: 2.1

If you're running windows, then the 1917Win.exe file should run on your machine.

If you're on Linux, the 1917Linux should run. You may have to run 'sudo chmod +x 1917Linux' to run file.

If you are stuck in the game, the 1917 Outline has all the details needed to complete the game.

This was created in two parts. Originally as a python game for CS1400 which is included in the repo.
Then i remade it in c++ for CS-3005 and have included a compiled version of it.
This c++ release is far better designed on the back end, the text readouts are much clearer, 
and other features were able to be added.


Thank you for Playing!

